# ---> Go
# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.env.local
*.pem

# ---> OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---> Frontend (Svelte + Vite)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Embedded SPA build output. Keep a placeholder committed: //go:embed fails to
# compile against a missing or empty directory, so a fresh clone must be able to
# `go build` before anyone has run Vite. vite.config.js sets emptyOutDir: false
# so the build does not delete these.
server/web/dist/*
!server/web/dist/.gitkeep
!server/web/dist/index.html

# ---> Runtime data volume: SQLite DB, downloaded assets, provider cache.
# Never commit. Scoped to the directory rather than *.db so test fixtures survive
# (Go fixtures live in testdata/ by convention, which this does not match).
# Unanchored on purpose: DATA_DIR defaults to ./data relative to the working
# directory, so `cd server && go run .` creates server/data/ — a leading-slash
# pattern would only have caught the repo root.
data/

# ---> Local binaries (`cd server && go build .` drops the binary in server/)
/sofalog
/server/sofalog
/bin/

# ---> Delve debug binaries: the VS Code Go debugger builds `__debug_bin<pid>`
# next to the package it launches. Unanchored so any package directory is covered.
__debug_bin*

# ---> Claude Code: commit settings.json, hooks, skills and commands;
# ignore only machine-local overrides.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---> Local folder that is not commited and contains files specific for the developer's environment
.local/

# ---> VS Code: commit the shared launch, task and extension recommendations;
# ignore personal settings and anything else the editor drops here.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
